schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Stakeholder education before crypto adoption
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    The practice of educating board/staff/donors on what crypto is and how
    donations would work before an org formally adopts crypto donations, so
    the eventual decision is informed rather than reactive.
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Framed in communicating-stakeholders.md as the mandatory first step, ahead
    of even a board vote — "not in depth, just enough to make an informed
    decision."
  adjacent_meanings:
    - change-management (general org practice of preparing stakeholders for a new capability)
  important_distinctions:
    - "education-before-adoption differs from marketing-after-adoption (the later donor-communication step)"
  tensions:
    - thoroughness-of-education vs board's-limited-attention-and-time
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating this as a one-time presentation rather than an ongoing readiness
    practice risks a board that nods along without real understanding of risk.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/communicating-stakeholders.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-a729337a8976
  source_lineage: communicating-stakeholders.md
